| `tests/integration/test_evals_gate.py` | Runs `scripts/run_evals.py --mode replay` twice in a scratch repository and fails unless both runs exit 0 with byte-identical passing reports and leave what git lists unchanged, and holds each refusal to its own exit code, so the eval harness is a writer that reaches a fixed point. | `make test` | [`evals.report_dir`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Replay only: it calls no model. Not the eval of the dataset: `make eval` runs that. | [README.md](../../evals/README.md) | always |
